# Call of Water for Horde Shamans: a trainer's letter -> Islen Waterseer south
# of Ratchet -> Brine's three waterskins (the Quilboar Watering Hole below her
# hut, the Spring Well in Tarren Mill, the Ruins of Stardust fountain in
# Ashenvale) -> Islen (Water Sapta) -> the Brazier of Everfount in Silverpine
# Forest -> Islen, who teaches Healing Stream Totem and gives the Water Totem.
# Sources: quests.json, npcs.json, objects.json and items.json (the fill
# objects); Forever's quest data for the rewards (quest 96: Healing Stream
# Totem and the Water Totem; 220: Water Sapta); Forever's quest notes for the
# places, the Razormane Pathfinder the brown skin calls (npc 3456, level 20),
# the Corrupt Minor Manifestation of Water (level 22, Frost Shock and Frost
# Nova, one spawn, 3 min 10 s respawn), the Ruins of Stardust island and the
# Sepulcher shortcut.
# The four openers (1528 Searn Firewarder in Orgrimmar, 1529 Xanis Flameweaver
# in Thunder Bluff, 2985 Swart in Razor Hill, 2986 Narm Skychaser in Bloodhoof
# Village) exclude one another; the steps take the city trainers' and hand in
# whichever letter you carry.
# Water Sapta (972, Islen) replaces a lost sapta while the brazier quest (63)
# is open; Tiev Mordune's Call of Water (1103) is the fallback when the
# Minor Manifestation of Water vanished before you spoke to it (TDB: after 63).
# The Horde leveling guides already carry this chain as class-only steps,
# spread from 20 to the low 30s (forever/horde/04-the-barrens to
# 30-40/02-thousand-needles); this guide does it in one go, for anyone off
# the route or wanting Healing Stream Totem sooner.

step Searn Firewarder
  only Orc,Troll
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip At 20 Searn Firewarder in the Valley of Wisdom sends you to Islen Waterseer in the Barrens. (Swart in Razor Hill gives the same letter: carry either.)
  level 20
  accept 1528 optional                        -- Searn Firewarder

step Xanis Flameweaver
  only Tauren,Skyborne
  zone Thunder Bluff
  tip At 20 Xanis Flameweaver, a shaman trainer on Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff, sends you to Islen Waterseer in the Barrens. (Narm Skychaser in Bloodhoof Village gives the same letter: carry either.)
  level 20
  accept 1529 optional                        -- Xanis Flameweaver

step Islen Waterseer
  zone The Barrens
  tip Islen is not in Ratchet: take the small coast road south from Ratchet past the pirate camp and over a low hill; her fishing hut, with a shark strung up outside, stands by the water before the pirate ship. If you reach the ship you went too far.
  goto 65.8,43.8 "Islen Waterseer"

step
  when onquest 1528
  turnin 1528                                 -- Islen Waterseer: Searn's letter

step
  when onquest 1529
  turnin 1529                                 -- Islen Waterseer: Xanis' letter

step
  when onquest 2985
  turnin 2985                                 -- Islen Waterseer: Swart's letter

step
  when onquest 2986
  turnin 2986                                 -- Islen Waterseer: Narm's letter

step Islen Waterseer
  accept 1530

step Brine
  tip Brine lives in the southern Barrens, south of Camp Taurajo: her hut sits on a hilltop of Blackthorn Ridge with a spinning windmill beside it, and the way up is the ridge by the lone tree. Quilboar camp all around the hill; Stormhides, thunderhawks and hyenas roam the plains on the way.
  turnin 1530                                 -- Brine
  accept 1535

step The Quilboar Watering Hole
  tip The muddy pond below Brine's hut. Step right into the puddle before you use the Empty Brown Waterskin (too far away and it refuses). Filling it calls a hostile Razormane Pathfinder (level 20): kill it, and watch for the quilboar hunter by the pond, who may start shooting afterwards.
  use 7766 quest 1535.1 @44.3,76.8            -- Empty Brown Waterskin, standing in the puddle
  collect 7769 quest 1535.1                   -- Filled Brown Waterskin

step Brine
  turnin 1535                                 -- Brine
  accept 1536

step The Spring Well
  zone Hillsbrad Foothills
  tip The Spring Well stands in the middle of Tarren Mill, just outside the church. From the Barrens: the zeppelin from Orgrimmar to Tirisfal Glades, then south past the Undercity and through Silverpine Forest (or fly once you have the Tarren Mill flight path). Hillsbrad is contested: Alliance players may attack. Stand beside the well and use the Empty Red Waterskin.
  use 7768 quest 1536.1 @62.2,20.8            -- Empty Red Waterskin, beside the well
  collect 7771 quest 1536.1                   -- Filled Red Waterskin

step Brine
  zone The Barrens
  turnin 1536                                 -- Brine
  accept 1534

step The Ruins of Stardust
  zone Ashenvale
  tip The right fountain stands in a ring of standing stones on the island of the small green lake south of Astranaar, west of Lake Mystral (not the island in Lake Mystral itself). From the Barrens take the road north through the Mor'shan Rampart and on west. Water elementals and walking treants guard the lake and root you in place; an elite Wandering Protector roams Ashenvale and can pass close by. Use the Empty Blue Waterskin beside the fountain.
  use 7767 quest 1534.1 @33.6,67.5            -- Empty Blue Waterskin, beside the fountain
  collect 7770 quest 1534.1                   -- Filled Blue Waterskin

step Brine
  zone The Barrens
  tip Back to Brine. She gives you the Vial of Purest Water for Islen.
  turnin 1534                                 -- Brine
  accept 220                                  -- the Vial of Purest Water, for Islen

step Islen Waterseer
  tip Islen hands you the Water Sapta and the Remaining Drops of Purest Water: take everything she offers before you leave for Silverpine, or you will be back for more.
  turnin 220 reward 6637                      -- Islen Waterseer: your Water Sapta
  accept 63

step Lost the Water Sapta?
  when onquest 63
  when !has 6637
  tip Only if the Water Sapta is gone from your bags: Islen gives you another.
  turnin 972 direct                           -- Islen Waterseer: a new Water Sapta

step The Brazier of Everfount
  zone Silverpine Forest
  tip Fly to the Sepulcher. The shrine lies in a hollow just south-west of it: go round the back of the crypt to the thick tree between the two hills, hop past it onto the rocks and drop west down the slope to the pool (each drop costs a little health). Drink the Water Sapta beside the tall standing stone by the pool: several water elementals appear, and only the corrupt one near the middle can be attacked (Tab picks it). The Corrupt Minor Manifestation of Water is level 22 and casts Frost Shock and Frost Nova; if someone just killed it, it is back in about three minutes. Its bracers always drop.
  use 6637 quest 63.1 @38.3,44.6              -- Water Sapta, beside the standing stone
  collect 7812 quest 63.1                     -- Corrupt Manifestation's Bracers

step The Minor Manifestation of Water
  tip Click the Brazier of Everfount to place the bracers and the drops. A few seconds later the pure Minor Manifestation of Water rises on the stone in the middle of the pool: speak to it while the Sapta Sight lasts (drink again by the stone if it has worn off). It gives you the Shard of Water for Islen. Gone before you could speak to it? Back at Islen ask for Call of Water (a fresh Water Sapta for Tiev Mordune, who stands just west of the shrine): hand it to Tiev, stay close while he calls the spirit back, then speak to it.
  turnin 63                                   -- Brazier of Everfount
  accept 100
  turnin 100                                  -- Minor Manifestation of Water
  accept 96

step Islen Waterseer
  zone The Barrens
  tip Back to Islen south of Ratchet. Keep the Water Totem in your bags for good: every water totem needs it.
  turnin 96 reward 5177                       -- Islen Waterseer: Healing Stream Totem and your Water Totem
